{title: The First Noel}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{columns: 2}

{start_of_verse: 1}
The [G]first No[D]el
The [C]angels did [G]say
Was to [C]certain poor
[G]Shepherds in [C]fields as [(D)]they [G]lay
In [G]fields where [D]they
Lay [C]keeping their [G]sheep
On a [C]cold winter's [G]night that [C]was [(D)]so [G]deep.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
No[G]el No[D]el, No[C]el No[G]el
[C]Born is the [G]King of [C]Is[(D)]ra[G]el.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
They [G]looked [D]up
And [C]saw a [G]star
Shining [C]in the [G]east be[C]yond [(D)]them [G]far
And [G]to the [D]earth
It [C]gave great [G]light
And [C]so it con[G]tinued both [C]day [(D)]and [G]night.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
And [G]by the [D]light
Of [C]that same [G]star
Three [C]wise men [G]came from [C]coun[(D)]try [G]far
To [G]seek for a [D]King
Was [C]their in[G]tent
And to [C]follow the [G]star wher[C]ever [(D)]it [G]went.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 4}
This [G]star drew [D]nigh
To [C]the north[G]west
O'er [C]Bethle[G]hem it [C]took [(D)]its [G]rest
And [G]there it [D]did
Both [C]stop and [G]stay
Right [C]over the [G]place where [C]Je[(D)]sus [G]lay.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: 5}
Then [G]entered [D]in
Those [C]wise men [G]three
Fell [C]reverent[G]ly u[C]pon [(D)]their [G]knee
And [G]offered [D]there
In [C]his pre[G]sence
Their [C]gold and [G]myrrh and [C]fran[(D)]kin[G]cense.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
